# DISABLED — host.biiquiz.com is now routed by Dokploy (Traefik), not host Nginx.
#
# Dokploy app: the "frontend" service from docker-compose.prod.yml, container port 3000.
# The frontend's own Next.js rewrite (frontend/next.config.mjs) already forwards /api/*
# to the backend container over the internal Docker network, so Dokploy's domain only
# needs to point at the frontend service — no separate /api/ rule is required.
#
# Matching action required on the server (not done by this repo change):
#   1. Confirm Dokploy's domain for host.biiquiz.com is verified and its TLS cert is issued.
#   2. sudo rm /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/host.biiquiz.com   (remove the symlink only)
#   3. sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
#   Keep /etc/nginx/sites-available/host.biiquiz.com as a backup for rollback.
#   Do not touch any other sites-enabled/sites-available file (e.g. hostapi.biiquiz.com).
#
